  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Look-Ka Py Py**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance; cut on the recording [3]\n- **Cissy Strut**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **Dazed and Confused , Hot For Teacher (intro guitar riff tease)**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **Inagodadavida**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **Hey Joe**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [3]\n- **Wonderful Tonight (Deaner on vocals)**: back after 240 archived shows (2663 days); mythic rare: 2 archived performances [3]\n- **Cocaine (Deaner on vocals)**: back after 65 archived shows (712 days); rare: 4 archived performances [3]\n- **One Way Out (Deaner on vocals)**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **Ween2008-07-13.BandOfBoognish** (recommended): source not stated; 12 songs; 73 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Gene did not play. The Hammond sat against the side wall, and its player apparently couldn't see the band [1]\n- The aftershow was in a small music store around the corner from the main venue, with a rowdy crowd [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **Ween2008-07-13.BandOfBoognish**: Recorded with MBHO603a capsules on a ka200, into an R4 at 24-bit/44.1, then dithered to 16-bit in Wavelab and encoded to FLAC [1]",
